title: Making a platform game
files: records.fathom
card: Chapter 17 | Making a game | Hop! A platform game that uses everything
say:
  Now let's put it all together, and make a real game: a platform game called Hop.
  A little blue block runs and jumps across floating platforms, picks up every coin, dodges spikes and bees, and reaches the flag at the end.
  It uses every part of the language we've seen. We'll write it piece by piece, and look closely at how each piece works.
uncard
open: records.fathom
say:
  The game keeps its best time in a second script, records dot fathom. It was written earlier. Let's read it first.
line: 16
zoom: lines 1-16
spot: lines 3-10
say:
  It uses seven libraries: encryption, hashing, json, big numbers, patterns, zip, time, and folders.
spot: lines 13-15
say:
  It remembers the best time, every point ever won, and a fingerprint of the level. Points ever is text, because it's a big number: it can grow without limit.
spot: off
line: 36
zoom: lines 18-36
spot: line 19
say:
  Fingerprint the level keeps a hash of the level. If the level ever changes, so does its fingerprint, and an old record won't be used for it.
spot: line 24
say:
  Load the record does nothing if there's no save file yet.
spot: line 26
say:
  The save file is encrypted, so nobody can change their best time by editing it. Decrypted with gives back the JSON text inside.
spot: line 27
say:
  A record for a different level raises a save problem, a kind of problem of our own.
spot: line 29
say:
  The pattern checks the points are only digits, as a big number must be.
spot: lines 32-35
say:
  A save problem says why the record was skipped. Any other problem, like a wrong password, is caught by the plain if that went wrong. Either way, the game starts fresh.
spot: off
line: 49
zoom: lines 38-49
spot: line 39
say:
  Save the record will run alongside the game, with meanwhile. Holding the lock makes sure two saves never mix.
spot: line 42
say:
  Big plus adds the new points to every point ever won.
spot: lines 43-46
say:
  The json changed at builds the record, one part at a time. Today, from the time library, is the date it was set.
spot: lines 47-48
say:
  Then it's encrypted into hop dot save, and a copy is packed into a zip file, as a backup.
spot: off
line: 61
zoom: lines 51-61
spot: lines 51-61
say:
  And a test: save a record, forget the best time, load it back, and check it's all there. Then the files are erased.
spot: off
zoom: out
test
zoom: output
say:
  The test passes. Now, the game.
wait
zoom: out
new: hop.fathom
paste:
  whisper: Hop! A small platformer. Left and right run, space jumps.
  whisper: Pick up every coin, keep away from the spikes and the bees, then touch the flag at the far end.

  use: window
  use: maths
  use: records.fathom

  a platform has:
    x (a number)
    y (a number)
    width (a number)
    height (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  a coin has:
    birth (a flat place)
  and the universe said i love you

  a spike has:
    x (a number)
    width (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  a bee has:
    birth (a flat place)
    reach (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  a queen bee is a kind of bee that has:
    crown (text)
  and the universe said i love you

  a danger is anything that can hurt and appear.

  a trail of anything has:
    items (a list of anything)
  and the universe said i love you
  
line: 17
zoom: lines 1-17
spot: lines 1-2
say:
  The top of the game says what it is, in whispers.
spot: lines 4-6
