say:
  A spike is a row of sharp points on the ground: where it starts, and how wide it is.
spot: lines 24-27
say:
  A bee has a birth, where its flight is centred, and a reach: how far it flies to each side.
spot: lines 29-31
say:
  A queen bee is a kind of bee, with a crown as well.
spot: line 33
say:
  A danger is anything that can hurt and appear. Spikes and bees are different kinds of things, but both will be dangers.
spot: lines 35-37
say:
  And a trail of anything keeps the last few of anything. The player will leave a trail of dust.
spot: off
